                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "u9ny8",
                      "name": "Column",
                      "width": 700,
                      "layout": "vertical",
                      "gap": 24,
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "NSOrV",
                          "name": "Measure Note",
                          "fill": "$text-muted",
                          "content": "OPTIMAL MEASURE · 680–720PX · ~75 CHARACTERS",
                          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
                          "fontSize": 10,
                          "fontWeight": "500",
                          "letterSpacing": 1.5
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "KEmWc",
                          "name": "H2",
                          "fill": "$text-primary",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "The case for product-driven engineering",
                          "lineHeight": 1.25,
                          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
                          "fontSize": 26,
                          "fontWeight": "700",
                          "letterSpacing": -0.5
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "ix5Ah",
                          "name": "P1",
                          "fill": "$text-secondary",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "For most of the last two decades, engineering and product operated as separate disciplines connected by a backlog. Requirements moved in one direction, and engineering's job was to implement them efficiently. That model scales poorly — it concentrates judgment in the wrong place and treats the people closest to the system as order-takers.",
                          "lineHeight": 1.7,
                          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
                          "fontSize": 18,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "GRElv",
                          "name": "P2",
                          "fill": "$text-secondary",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "The organizations that compound advantage do the opposite. They give engineers genuine ownership of outcomes, not just output, and they make product judgment a shared competency rather than a gate.",
                          "lineHeight": 1.7,
                          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
                          "fontSize": 18,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "frame",
                          "id": "a1PoSO",
                          "name": "Pull Quote",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "stroke": "$border-accent",
                          "strokeWidth": {
                            "left": 3
                          },
                          "strokeAlignment": "inner",
                          "layout": "vertical",
                          "padding": [
                            8,
                            28
                          ],
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "h2S3f6",
                              "name": "Q",
                              "fill": "$text-primary",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": "fill_container",
                              "content": "The best engineering organizations don't wait for product to hand them requirements — they participate in shaping them.",
                              "lineHeight": 1.5,
                              "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
                              "fontSize": 21,
                              "fontWeight": "500",
                              "fontStyle": "italic"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "rTq0G",
                          "name": "H3",
                          "fill": "$text-primary",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "What this looks like in practice",
                          "lineHeight": 1.3,
                          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
                          "fontSize": 20,
                          "fontWeight": "600",
                          "letterSpacing": -0.25
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "F7EanC",
                          "name": "P3",
                          "fill": "$text-secondary",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "It starts with how teams are framed. Instead of assigning features, you assign problems and the metrics that define success — then hold the team accountable for the result, not the ticket count.",
                          "lineHeight": 1.7,
                          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
                          "fontSize": 18,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "frame",
                          "id": "yNQDt",
                          "name": "List",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "layout": "vertical",
                          "gap": 10,
                          "padding": [
                            4,
                            0,
                            0,
                            0
                          ],
                          "children": [
                            {
